Extreme heat is increasingly becoming a persistent silent killer in Europe. This year’s heatwaves have shown that heat lacks the visible devastation of floods or storms, yet it quietly worsens cardiovascular, renal and mental-health risks (see Nature 655, 288–290; 2026). It also increases pressure on health-care systems.


